        "source": "Canonical PALACE v1.0 pmd_refcont.dat fcHO2 and fcFeO interpolated onto the native LVM grid, with fcO2Ac taken verbatim from the native-LVM joint diffuse refit",
        "why": "Canonical fcHO2/fcFeO restore PALACE's species identification -- FeO peaks at 5966 A (Noll+24 put FeO(VIS) at 595 nm) and HO2 is the blue tail of the 1.51 um feature -- while the refit fcO2Ac keeps the blue. Canonical O2Ac peaks at 3220 A, outside the LVM band, so only its tail is in range and it runs ~2x high through 4200-5900 A. Measured on 10 far-arm dark off-ecliptic rows: fully canonical costs x1.43 in blue chi2 and biases the median pull to -0.26; the hybrid recovers that to -0.02 and has the best full-band chi2 of the three.",
